    {
      "id": "s0002",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "13 Invoking diff ¶",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The format for running the [[p0]] command is:",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "diff"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "In the simplest case, two file names [[p0]] and [[p1]] are given, and [[p2]] compares the contents of [[p3]] and [[p4]]. A file name of [[p5]] stands for the standard input.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "from-file"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "to-file"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "diff"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "from-file"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "text": "to-file"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p5]]",
          "text": "-"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If one file is a directory and the other is not, [[p0]] compares the file in the directory whose name is that of the non-directory. The non-directory file must not be [[p1]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "diff"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "-"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If two file names are given and both are directories, [[p0]] compares corresponding files in both directories, in alphabetical order; this comparison is not recursive unless the [[p1]] ([[p2]]) option is given. [[p3]] never compares the actual contents of a directory as if it were a file. The file that is fully specified may not be standard input, because standard input is nameless and the notion of “file with the same name” does not apply.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "diff"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "--recursive"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "-r"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "diff"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If the [[p0]] option is given, the number of file names is arbitrary, and [[p1]] is compared to each named file. Similarly, if the [[p2]] option is given, each named file is compared to [[p3]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--from-file=file"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "file"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "--to-file=file"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "file"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]] options begin with ‘[[p1]]’, so normally file names may not begin with ‘[[p2]]’. However, [[p3]] as an argument by itself treats the remaining arguments as file names even if they begin with ‘[[p4]]’.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "diff"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "-"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "-"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "--"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "text": "-"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "An exit status of 0 means no differences were found, 1 means some differences were found, and 2 means trouble.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Options to diff"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Up: [[p0]] [[[p1]]][[[p2]]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Invoking diff"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "Contents"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "Index"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0012",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "13.1 Options to diff ¶",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Below is a summary of all of the options that GNU [[p0]] accepts. Most options have two equivalent names, one of which is a single letter preceded by ‘[[p1]]’, and the other of which is a long name preceded by ‘[[p2]]’. Multiple single letter options (unless they take an argument) can be combined into a single command line word: [[p3]] is equivalent to [[p4]]. Long named options can be abbreviated to any unique prefix of their name. Brackets ([ and ]) indicate that an option takes an optional argument.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "diff"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "-"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "--"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "-ac"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "text": "-a -c"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0014",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-a"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0015",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0016",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Treat all files as text and compare them line-by-line, even if they do not seem to be text. See [[p0]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Binary Files and Forcing Text Comparisons"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0017",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-b"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0018",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--ignore-space-change"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0019",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ignore changes in amount of white space. See [[p0]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Suppressing Differences in Blank and Tab Spacing"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0020",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-B"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0021",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--ignore-blank-lines"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0022",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ignore changes that just insert or delete blank lines. See [[p0]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Suppressing Differences Whose Lines Are All Blank"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0023",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--binary"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0024",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Read and write data in binary mode. See [[p0]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Binary Files and Forcing Text Comparisons"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0025",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-c"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0026",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Use the context output format, showing three lines of context. See [[p0]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Context Format"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0027",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--color [=when]"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "¶"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0028",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Specify whether to use color for distinguishing different contexts, like header, added or removed lines. [[p0]] may be omitted, or one of:",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "when"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0029",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "none Do not use color at all. This is the default when no –color option is specified.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0030",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "auto Use color only if standard output is a terminal.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0031",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "always Always use color.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0032",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Specifying [[p0]] and no [[p1]] is equivalent to [[p2]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--color"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "when"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "--color=auto"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0033",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-C lines"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0034",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--context[=lines]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0035",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Use the context output format, showing [[p0]] (an integer) lines of context, or three if [[p1]] is not given. See [[p2]]. For proper operation, [[p3]] typically needs at least two lines of context.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "lines"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "lines"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "Context Format"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "patch"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0036",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "For compatibility [[p0]] also supports an obsolete option syntax [[p1]] that has effect when combined with [[p2]], [[p3]], or [[p4]]. New scripts should use [[p5]] ([[p6]]) instead.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "diff"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "-lines"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "-c"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "-p"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "text": "-u"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p5]]",
          "text": "-U lines"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p6]]",
          "text": "-C lines"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0037",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--changed-group-format=format"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0038",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Use [[p0]] to output a line group containing differing lines from both files in if-then-else format. See [[p1]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "format"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "Line Group Formats"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0039",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-d"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0040",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--minimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0041",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Change the algorithm perhaps find a smaller set of changes. This makes [[p0]] slower (sometimes much slower). See [[p1]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "diff"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "diff Performance Tradeoffs"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0042",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-D name"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0043",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--ifdef=name"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0044",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Make merged ‘[[p0]]’ format output, conditional on the preprocessor macro [[p1]]. See [[p2]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "#ifdef"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "name"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "Merging Files with If-then-else"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0045",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-e"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0046",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--ed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0047",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Make output that is a valid [[p0]] script. See [[p1]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "ed"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "ed Scripts"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0048",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-E"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0049",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--ignore-tab-expansion"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0050",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ignore changes due to tab expansion. See [[p0]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Suppressing Differences in Blank and Tab Spacing"
